detailedExplanation.whatItIs:
Structured output pairs a schema with the request so the model returns conforming data. For example, given a schema like:
{"type": "object", "properties": {"city": {"type": "string"}, "temp_c": {"type": "number"}}, "required": ["city", "temp_c"]}
the model returns {"city": "Paris", "temp_c": 18} rather than a prose sentence.

A tool schema declares a callable interface. For example:
{
  "name": "get_weather",
  "description": "Get the current weather for a city.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {"city": {"type": "string", "description": "City name"}},
    "required": ["city"]
  }
}
The model reads this to decide when and how to call the tool.
